inode/directory — a directory's content IS its entries.

So `edit` is the file manager: renaming, moving and deleting are editing
the listing. There is no file-manager program. Identity comes from the
qid tracked through the edit stream, not from a visible column, so a
rename is never mistaken for a delete-plus-create.

Nothing happens until Save; the status line shows the plan continuously
("pending 3 renames, 1 delete"); and `#V` snapshots make a destructive
save genuinely reversible.
